            System.out.println("String text uploaded successfully!");
        } else {
            System.out.println("Failed to upload string text. Response code: " + responseCode);
        }

        connection.disconnect();
    }
}
```

In this code, the `URLConnection.guessContentTypeFromName(fileName)` method is used to determine the content type based on the file extension of the given file name. If the content type cannot be determined, it defaults to `"application/octet-stream"` which is a generic binary data content type. You can replace `"example.txt"` with the actual file name and adjust the `textToUpload` variable as needed.

