To create a graph collection in Java and store the data in MongoDB, you can follow these steps:

1. **Define Graph Data Structures**: Define the classes for the graph, including nodes (vertices) and edges.

2. **Use MongoDB Java Driver**: Use the MongoDB Java driver to interact with MongoDB.

3. **Store and Retrieve Data**: Store and retrieve graph data in MongoDB using the defined structures.

Below is an example implementation:

### Step 1: Define Graph Data Structures

```java
import java.util.*;

class Node {
    String id;
    String value;
    List<Edge> edges;

    public Node(String id, String value) {
        this.id = id;
        this.value = value;
        this.edges = new ArrayList<>();
    }
}

class Edge {
    String from;
    String to;
    int weight;

    public Edge(String from, String to, int weight) {
        this.from = from;
        this.to = to;
        this.weight = weight;
    }
}

class Graph {
    Map<String, Node> nodes;

    public Graph() {
        this.nodes = new HashMap<>();
    }

    public void addNode(String id, String value) {
        nodes.put(id, new Node(id, value));
    }

    public void addEdge(String from, String to, int weight) {
        Node fromNode = nodes.get(from);
        Node toNode = nodes.get(to);
        if (fromNode != null && toNode != null) {
            fromNode.edges.add(new Edge(from, to, weight));
        }
    }

    public Node getNode(String id) {
        return nodes.get(id);
    }
}
```

### Step 2: Use MongoDB Java Driver

Add the MongoDB Java driver dependency to your `pom.xml` if you're using Maven:

```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.mongodb</groupId>
    <artifactId>mongodb-driver-sync</artifactId>
    <version>4.3.2</version>
</dependency>
```

### Step 3: Store and Retrieve Data

```java
import com.mongodb.client.*;
import org.bson.Document;
import com.mongodb.client.model.Filters;

import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class GraphMongoDB {
    private static final String DATABASE_NAME = "graphDB";
    private static final String COLLECTION_NAME = "graph";

    private MongoClient mongoClient;
    private MongoDatabase database;
    private MongoCollection<Document> collection;

    public GraphMongoDB() {
        mongoClient = MongoClients.create("mongodb://localhost:27017");
        database = mongoClient.getDatabase(DATABASE_NAME);
        collection = database.getCollection(COLLECTION_NAME);
    }

    public void insertGraph(Graph graph) {
        for (Node node : graph.nodes.values()) {
            Document nodeDoc = new Document("id", node.id)
                    .append("value", node.value)
                    .append("edges", new ArrayList<Document>());

            for (Edge edge : node.edges) {
                Document edgeDoc = new Document("from", edge.from)
                        .append("to", edge.to)
                        .append("weight", edge.weight);
                nodeDoc.getList("edges", Document.class).add(edgeDoc);
            }

            collection.insertOne(nodeDoc);
        }
    }

    public Graph getGraph() {
        Graph graph = new Graph();
        FindIterable<Document> docs = collection.find();

        for (Document doc : docs) {
            String id = doc.getString("id");
            String value = doc.getString("value");
            graph.addNode(id, value);

            List<Document> edges = doc.getList("edges", Document.class);
            for (Document edgeDoc : edges) {
                String from = edgeDoc.getString("from");
                String to = edgeDoc.getString("to");
                int weight = edgeDoc.getInteger("weight");
                graph.addEdge(from, to, weight);
            }
        }

        return graph;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        GraphMongoDB graphMongoDB = new GraphMongoDB();

        // Create a new graph
        Graph graph = new Graph();
        graph.addNode("1", "A");
        graph.addNode("2", "B");
        graph.addNode("3", "C");
        graph.addEdge("1", "2", 5);
        graph.addEdge("2", "3", 3);
        graph.addEdge("1", "3", 9);

        // Insert the graph into MongoDB
        graphMongoDB.insertGraph(graph);

        // Retrieve the graph from MongoDB
        Graph retrievedGraph = graphMongoDB.getGraph();
        System.out.println("Retrieved graph nodes:");
        for (Node node : retrievedGraph.nodes.values()) {
            System.out.println("Node ID: " + node.id + ", Value: " + node.value);
            for (Edge edge : node.edges) {
                System.out.println("  Edge from " + edge.from + " to " + edge.to + " with weight " + edge.weight);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

