2. **Write the Java Code:**
   Create a service class that checks for files in the specified folder, renames them with a timestamp, and then moves them to an "archive" subfolder.

   ```java
   import com.amazonaws.services.s3.AmazonS3;
   import com.amazonaws.services.s3.AmazonS3ClientBuilder;
   import com.amazonaws.services.s3.model.CopyObjectRequest;
   import com.amazonaws.services.s3.model.ObjectListing;
   import com.amazonaws.services.s3.model.S3ObjectSummary;

   import java.text.SimpleDateFormat;
   import java.util.Date;
   import java.util.List;

   import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Value;
   import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;

   @Service
   public class S3FileManagementService {

       @Value("${aws.accessKeyId}")
       private String awsAccessKeyId;

       @Value("${aws.secretKey}")
       private String awsSecretKey;

       @Value("${aws.s3.bucketName}")
       private String bucketName;

       public void processFilesInFolder() {
           AmazonS3 s3Client = AmazonS3ClientBuilder
                   .standard()
                   .withCredentials(new AWSStaticCredentialsProvider(new BasicAWSCredentials(awsAccessKeyId, awsSecretKey)))
                   .build();

           String sourceFolderKey = "your-source-folder/"; // Change this to your source folder key
           String archiveFolderKey = "your-source-folder/archive/"; // Change this to your archive folder key
           ObjectListing objectListing = s3Client.listObjects(bucketName, sourceFolderKey);
           List<S3ObjectSummary> objectSummaries = objectListing.getObjectSummaries();

           SimpleDateFormat sdf = new SimpleDateFormat("yyyyMMddHHmmss");

           for (S3ObjectSummary objectSummary : objectSummaries) {
               String sourceKey = objectSummary.getKey();
               String fileName = sourceKey.substring(sourceKey.lastIndexOf("/") + 1);
               String newFileName = sdf.format(new Date()) + "_" + fileName;

               s3Client.copyObject(
                       bucketName,
                       sourceKey,
                       bucketName,
                       archiveFolderKey + newFileName
               );

               s3Client.deleteObject(bucketName, sourceKey);
           }
       }
   }
   ```

3. **Trigger the Process:**
   You can trigger the `processFilesInFolder` method from a controller or a scheduled task, depending on when you want to perform this operation.

