Yes, using `useMemo` is an excellent choice for optimizing the calculation of `catTreeList` and `qIdMap`. By doing so, you ensure that these values are only recalculated when the `data` changes, which can improve performance by avoiding unnecessary computations on each render.

Here's how you can refactor the `InterviewMgmtProvider` component to use `useMemo`:

```javascript
import React, { createContext, useContext, useEffect, useMemo } from 'react';
import { useDispatch, useSelector } from 'react-redux';
import { fetchCategoryTree } from '../../../redux/slices/interviewMgmtSlice';

const InterviewMgmtContext = createContext();

export const InterviewMgmtProvider = ({ children }) => {
  const dispatch = useDispatch();
  const selectedTreeNodeUID = useSelector(
    (state) => state.interviewMgmt.selectedTreeNodeUID
  );
  const data = useSelector((state) => state.interviewMgmt.data);

  useEffect(() => {
    dispatch(fetchCategoryTree());
  }, [dispatch]);

  const catTreeList = useMemo(() => {
    if (data.length > 0) {
      return data.map((c) => ({
        id: c.uniqueId,
        name: c.heading,
        type: 'category',
        children: c.questions?.map((q) => ({
          id: q.uniqueId,
          name: q.heading,
          type: 'question',
        })) || [],
      }));
    }
    return [];
  }, [data]);

  const qIdMap = useMemo(() => {
    if (data.length > 0) {
      return data.flatMap((category) =>
        category.questions?.map((question) => ({
          categoryUniqueId: category.uniqueId,
          questionUniqueId: question.uniqueId,
        })) || []
      );
    }
    return [];
  }, [data]);

  return (
    <InterviewMgmtContext.Provider
      value={{ catTreeList, qIdMap, selectedTreeNodeUID }}
    >
      {children}
    </InterviewMgmtContext.Provider>
  );
};

export const useInterviewMgmt = () => {
  return useContext(InterviewMgmtContext);
};
```

### Explanation:
- **`useMemo`**: The `useMemo` hook is used to memoize the results of `catTreeList` and `qIdMap` so that they are only recomputed when `data` changes.
- **Performance**: This approach avoids unnecessary recalculations of `catTreeList` and `qIdMap` on every render, which can be beneficial if the data processing is complex or if the component re-renders frequently.

This change should enhance the efficiency of your component, especially as your application scales.

