GET http://localhost:8080/secure
Headers: Authorization: Bearer <admin_token>
```

- Accessing the secure endpoint without the required role:
```
GET http://localhost:8080/secure
Headers: Authorization: Bearer <user_token>
```

- Accessing the public endpoint:
```
GET http://localhost:8080/public
```

Remember to replace `<admin_token>` and `<user_token>` with valid authentication tokens. This example assumes the use of OAuth 2.0 or JWT for authentication and authorization, but you can adapt it to your specific authentication mechanism.

