MongoDB replica sets rely on being able to reliably figure out the domain name for each member.  
On Linux and OSX, the MongoDB server uses the output of the 【69†hostname command†linux.die.net】 to figure out the domain name to report to the replica set. This can cause confusing errors if you're connecting to a remote MongoDB replica set running on a machine that reports its `hostname` as `localhost`:

