This will create a new Next.js project in the `my-nextjs-app` directory and start the development server. You can then visit `http://localhost:3000` in your web browser to see the application running, displaying the text "Welcome to My Next.js App!" and a paragraph below it.

You can use `fetch` API or libraries like Axios to consume the backend API endpoint from your Next.js frontend. Here's an example using `fetch`:

```javascript
// pages/index.js

import React, { useState } from 'react';

const Home = () => {
  const [userData, setUserData] = useState({ name: '', email: '' });

  const handleChange = (e) => {
    const { name, value } = e.target;
    setUserData({ ...userData, [name]: value });
  };

  const handleSubmit = async (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();

    try {
      const response = await fetch('http://localhost:8080/api/user', {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: {
          'Content-Type': 'application/json',
        },
        body: JSON.stringify(userData),
      });

      if (response.ok) {
        console.log('User data saved successfully!');
        // Clear the form
        setUserData({ name: '', email: '' });
      } else {
        console.error('Failed to save user data');
      }
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Error:', error);
    }
  };

  return (
    <div>
      <h1>Welcome to My Next.js App!</h1>
      <form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>
        <label>
          Name:
          <input
            type="text"
            name="name"
            value={userData.name}
            onChange={handleChange}
          />
        </label>
        <br />
        <label>
          Email:
          <input
            type="email"
            name="email"
            value={userData.email}
            onChange={handleChange}
          />
        </label>
        <br />
        <button type="submit">Save</button>
      </form>
    </div>
  );
};

export default Home;
```

In this example:

- We define a form with input fields for name and email.
- We use `useState` hook to manage the form data.
- `handleChange` function updates the form data as the user types.
- `handleSubmit` function is called when the form is submitted. It sends a POST request to `http://localhost:8080/api/user` with the user data.
- If the request is successful, it clears the form. Otherwise, it logs an error.

Make sure to replace `http://localhost:8080/api/user` with your actual backend endpoint.

