To implement all CRUD operations (Create, Read, Update, Delete) in a `dataSlice` using Redux Toolkit, you'll need to define additional actions and reducers. Below is a comprehensive `dataSlice` that handles all CRUD operations.

Assuming you have already set up the server with appropriate endpoints for each CRUD operation, here's the complete `dataSlice.js` file:

```js
// redux/dataSlice.js
import { createSlice, createAsyncThunk } from '@reduxjs/toolkit';
import axios from 'axios';

// Replace 'your-api-base-url' with your actual API base URL.
const API_BASE_URL = 'http://localhost:5000/api';

// Async Thunks for CRUD Operations

// Fetch all data from the server
export const fetchData = createAsyncThunk('data/fetchData', async () => {
  const response = await axios.get(`${API_BASE_URL}/get-data`);
  return response.data;
});

// Save new data to the server
export const saveData = createAsyncThunk('data/saveData', async (newData) => {
  const response = await axios.post(`${API_BASE_URL}/add-data`, newData);
  return response.data;
});

// Update data on the server
export const updateData = createAsyncThunk('data/updateData', async (updatedData) => {
  const response = await axios.put(`${API_BASE_URL}/update-data/${updatedData.id}`, updatedData);
  return response.data;
});

// Delete data from the server
export const deleteData = createAsyncThunk('data/deleteData', async (id) => {
  const response = await axios.delete(`${API_BASE_URL}/delete-data/${id}`);
  return id;
});

const dataSlice = createSlice({
  name: 'data',
  initialState: [],
  reducers: {},
  extraReducers: (builder) => {
    builder
      // Handle the fetch data success case
      .addCase(fetchData.fulfilled, (state, action) => {
        return action.payload;
      })
      // Handle the save data success case
      .addCase(saveData.fulfilled, (state, action) => {
        state.push(action.payload);
      })
      // Handle the update data success case
      .addCase(updateData.fulfilled, (state, action) => {
        const updatedData = action.payload;
        const index = state.findIndex(item => item.id === updatedData.id);
        if (index !== -1) {
          state[index] = updatedData;
        }
      })
      // Handle the delete data success case
      .addCase(deleteData.fulfilled, (state, action) => {
        const id = action.payload;
        return state.filter(item => item.id !== id);
      });
  },
});

export default dataSlice.reducer;
```

In this `dataSlice.js`, we've defined four async thunks for each CRUD operation (`fetchData`, `saveData`, `updateData`, and `deleteData`). These async thunks make API calls using Axios to interact with the server.

The `extraReducers` section handles the success cases of each async thunk and updates the state accordingly. For example, after successfully fetching data from the server, the `fetchData.fulfilled` case updates the state with the fetched data. Similarly, for save, update, and delete operations, the relevant data is updated in the state based on the server's response.

To use these async thunks in your components, you can dispatch them using the `useDispatch` hook from `react-redux`. For example:

```jsx
import { useDispatch } from 'react-redux';
import { fetchData, saveData, updateData, deleteData } from './redux/dataSlice';

// Inside your component...
const dispatch = useDispatch();

// Fetch data
dispatch(fetchData());

// Save data
const newData = { date: '2023-07-25', title: 'New Data', htmlText: 'Sample HTML text' };
dispatch(saveData(newData));

// Update data
const updatedData = { id: 'your-item-id', date: '2023-07-26', title: 'Updated Data', htmlText: 'Updated HTML text' };
dispatch(updateData(updatedData));

// Delete data
const itemIdToDelete = 'your-item-id-to-delete';
dispatch(deleteData(itemIdToDelete));
```

Remember to configure your server endpoints to handle the respective CRUD operations and to replace `'your-api-base-url'` in the `API_BASE_URL` constant with your actual API base URL.

