To set CORS headers in Nginx, you can use the `add_header` directive to add the necessary headers to responses. Here's how you can configure Nginx to allow requests from `http://localhost:3002` for the `/words` endpoint:

```nginx
http {
    # Other Nginx configuration...

    server {
        listen 80;
        server_name localhost;

        location /words {
            add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' 'http://localhost:3002';
            add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Methods' 'GET, POST, PUT, DELETE';
            add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Headers' 'Content-Type, Authorization';

            # Proxy pass to your backend service
            proxy_pass http://backend_service;
        }

        # Other location blocks for different endpoints...
    }
}
```

In this configuration:

- The `location /words` block specifies the endpoint for which CORS headers are being configured.
